class=\"strong\">must</span> are modals.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "I should go to the gym for an hour after work, but I sometimes do activities when we're at port.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I often read the newspaper, or I could go for a jog before work.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I must wake up early. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Sometimes I have to buy ingredients or research new recipes in the afternoon. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<br/><br/>You use <span class = \"italic\"> should, could</span> and<span class = \"italic\">  might</span> to give advice, show possibility or expectation, or make a suggestion.<br/><br/> You use <span class = \"italic\"> have to</span> and <span class = \"italic\"> must</span> to show obligation. <br/><br/>The modals are followed by a verb in the base form. The verb does not change.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Be Going To and Present Continuous Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "The structure be<span class=\"strong\"> going to + verb</span> and the Present Continuous tense are similar. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "I'm staying in New York for two weeks. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'm going to stay in New York for a while. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We're visiting Baja, California until November 5th.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We're going to visit Baja, California sometime next year. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They can be used to talk about the future.<br/><br/>You use the structure<span class = \"italic\"> be going to + verb</span> to talk about future intentions or decisions in a general way.<br/><br/>You use the Present Continuous tense for future plans or arrangements that are planned or booked.", "type": "text"}]}, {"content": "engenn4le12ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "festivity ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "public events or